# KnowledgeForge E2E Testing - Pytest/Testing Project Rules

## 🚀 MANDATORY REGRESSION CHECK
- **IMPORTANT**: After any change to tests or extraction, run `make quick-check` from the project root.
- Maintain the 11/11 passing status of the extraction benchmark.

## 🧪 E2E Objectives
- Validate C4 metadata extraction (Owner, Tier, Status, etc.).
- Validate Service URL/Endpoint extraction.
- Validate ReactFlow-compatible JSON structure.

## Core Principles
- Write comprehensive end-to-end tests that validate the complete user workflow
- Test real integrations between UI, API, and databases (Neo4j, metadata store)
- Focus on critical user paths and error scenarios
- Ensure tests are reliable, maintainable, and provide clear feedback
- Use proper test fixtures and helpers for consistent test environments

## Testing Standards
- Use pytest with async support for all test cases
- Follow AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert in test structure
- Use descriptive test names that explain the scenario being tested
- Group related tests in classes with clear setup/teardown methods
- Validate both happy path and error conditions
- Test data integrity across all system components

## File Organization
- **NEVER create empty folders or placeholder files without explicit permission**
- Use lowercase for all folder names (e.g., test-data/, fixtures/)
- Use lowercase for all file names (e.g., test_pipeline.py, conftest.py)
- Ask user before creating new directories or major structural changes
- Place test fixtures in conftest.py for reusability
- Create helper classes in test_helpers.py for common operations
- Keep test data and CSV samples organized and documented
- Use clear naming conventions for test files: test_<feature>_<scenario>.py

## Test Structure & Patterns
- Use pytest fixtures for database connections, test clients, and sample data
- Implement proper cleanup in fixtures to ensure test isolation
- Use async/await properly for API calls and database operations
- Mock external dependencies when needed but prefer real integrations for E2E tests
- Validate responses at multiple levels: HTTP status, data structure, database state

## Database Testing
- Use separate test databases or in-memory databases when possible
- Clean up test data before and after each test
- Verify data persistence and consistency across components
- Test both successful operations and rollback scenarios
- Validate graph relationships and metadata storage

## API Testing
- Test complete request/response cycles including file uploads
- Validate error handling and proper HTTP status codes
- Test authentication and authorization if applicable
- Verify background task completion and status tracking
- Test WebSocket connections if used

## Code Quality
- Use type hints for all function parameters and return values
- Handle async operations properly with proper error handling
- Use context managers for resource management (files, database connections)
- Write clear assertion messages that help debug failures
- Include timeouts for operations that might hang

## Documentation
- Document complex test scenarios and their purpose
- Include setup instructions in README files
- Document required services and their configuration
- Explain test data requirements and generation
- Document known limitations or test environment dependencies

## Performance & Reliability
- Set appropriate timeouts for async operations
- Use retry mechanisms for flaky external dependencies
- Implement proper wait conditions for async operations
- Monitor test execution time and identify slow tests
- Use parallel execution when tests are independent

## Environment Management
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Support multiple test environments (local, CI, staging)
- Isolate test runs to prevent interference
- Clean up temporary files and test artifacts
- Document required environment setup

## Error Handling & Debugging
- Provide clear error messages in test failures
- Log important intermediate states for debugging
- Use proper exception handling in test setup/teardown
- Include diagnostic information in test reports
- Support debug mode for detailed logging

## CI/CD Integration
- Ensure tests run reliably in CI environments
- Support test result reporting and coverage metrics
- Handle test environment setup and teardown
- Fail fast on critical errors but complete full test suites
- Generate artifacts for test analysis
